<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">4 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 4 October, from 23 to 1965.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/lulin" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lulin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/23">23 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">2,003 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lülin rebels sack Chang'an, the capital of Wang Mang's Xin dynasty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lulin">Lülin</a> peasant rebellion, rebels captured and sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a>, capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-mang">Wang Mang</a>'s short-lived <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xin-dynasty">Xin dynasty</a>; Wang Mang was killed two days later. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Eastern Han</a> government later made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a> its primary capital.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lulin">Lülin</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1209">1209 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">817 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Innocent III crowns Otto IV emperor in Rome</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Otto IV of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-welf">Welf dynasty</a>, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-lion">Henry the Lion</a> and king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> since 1198, was crowned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-innocent-iii">Pope Innocent III</a>. He later broke with the pope and lost power after Bouvines in 1214.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-iv-holy-roman-emperor">Otto IV, Holy Roman Emperor</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-innocent-iii">Pope Innocent III</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1363">1363 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">663 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Zhu Yuanzhang wins the Battle of Lake Poyang</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-poyang">Lake Poyang</a>, the smaller fleet of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hongwu-emperor">Zhu Yuanzhang</a> destroyed the tower ships of his rival <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chen-youliang">Chen Youliang</a> with fire ships, and Chen was killed by an arrow. The victory made Zhu, the future Hongwu Emperor, master of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lake-poyang">Battle of Lake Poyang</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hongwu-emperor">Hongwu Emperor</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chen-youliang">Chen Youliang</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1448">1448 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">578 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Skanderbeg and Venice make peace, ending the Albanian–Venetian War</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skanderbeg">Skanderbeg</a> and the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> signed a peace negotiated by Georgius Pelino. Venice kept Dagnum but ceded Buzëgjarpri, at the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drin">Drin</a>, agreed to pay Skanderbeg 1,400 ducats and let him buy salt tax-free from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durres">Durazzo</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skanderbeg">Skanderbeg</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1582">1582 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">444 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Catholic Europe switches to the Gregorian calendar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, Portugal and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, Thursday 4 October 1582 was followed directly by Friday 15 October. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-xiii">Pope Gregory XIII</a>'s reform dropped ten days to realign the calendar with the solar year.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1830">1830 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">196 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Belgium's provisional government declares independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Following the September uprising in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>'s provisional government declared independence from the United <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Kingdom of the Netherlands</a>. The great powers recognised the new state, and later guaranteed its neutrality.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Kingdom of the Netherlands</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1957">1957 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">69 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Soviet Union launches Sputnik 1</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> placed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sputnik-1">Sputnik 1</a>, an 84-kilogram metal sphere, into orbit, the first artificial satellite. Its radio beeps, picked up worldwide, shocked the West and launched the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/space-race">Space Race</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1965">1965 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">61 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Paul VI becomes the first pope to visit the United States</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Pope Paul VI flew to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> for a one-day visit, the first by a reigning pope to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. He appealed for peace at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations-general-assembly">United Nations General Assembly</a> and celebrated Mass at Yankee Stadium.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 4 October <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francisco-jose-de-caldas"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francisco-jose-de-caldas.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Francisco José de Caldas</span><span class="tp">1768–1816</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francois-guizot"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francois-guizot.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">François Guizot</span><span class="tp">1787–1874</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/marcelo-t-de-alvear"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/marcelo-t-de-alvear.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Marcelo T. de Alvear</span><span class="tp">1868–1942</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/engelbert-dollfuss"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/engelbert-dollfuss.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Engelbert Dollfuss</span><span class="tp">1892–1934</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 4 October <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/rembrandt"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/rembrandt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Rembrandt</span><span class="tp">1606–1669</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alexandros-papagos"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alexandros-papagos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alexandros Papagos</span><span class="tp">1883–1955</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pyotr-masherov"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pyotr-masherov.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pyotr Masherov</span><span class="tp">1918–1980</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jean-claude-duvalier"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jean-claude-duvalier.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jean-Claude Duvalier</span><span class="tp">1951–2014</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
